HIRAX Maxwell scattering (MATLAB)
================================

The current implementation is organized in the leaves module:

  leaves/geometry/         four-leaf surfaces and patch utilities
  leaves/quadrature/       corrected quadrature and C4 symmetry reuse
  leaves/solver/           complete NRCCIE operator and direct RS-S solves
  leaves/skeletonization/  incoming/outgoing compression and scattering matrix
  leaves/test/             scattering-matrix example and new run results

Place fmm3dbie-hirax-dev, FLAM, chunkie, and the HIRAX strong-skel fork next
to this repository (or set NRCCIE_DEPENDENCY_ROOT):

  https://github.com/wangyuguan/strong-skel

Use commit 2c27790db9a23c92c399ce5a9c0ef1dba784fd4e, which supplies the
deterministic empty-proxy mode and the asymmetric multiply/solve routines.
See ../strong-skel/README.md for attribution and the compatibility regression.

Run startup.m to initialize dependencies and the leaves MATLAB paths.
From the repository root, the current entry point is:

  matlab -batch "run('leaves/test/nrccie_scattering_matrix_leaf.m')"

See leaves/README for the numerical method, parameters, validation, and
saved scattering-matrix interface. Existing local results and diagnostic
archives remain in their original locations.

A separate small ellipsoid example tests the square sphere-to-sphere
Maxwell scattering interface and Stratton-Chu target evaluation:

  run('startup.m')
  result = test_ellipsoid_scattering(16,20);

See test/ellipsoid/README for the construction, trace layout, and validation.
With that result saved, run test_ellipsoid_shared_skeleton(1e-8) to select
common incoming/outgoing sphere points and test a square compressed matrix.
To construct a square compressed matrix directly from B and C, without the
full scattering matrix, run test_ellipsoid_bc_skeleton(1e-6). This interface
uses projected incoming coefficients; see test/ellipsoid/README.

The complete toy-array rehearsal uses four small closed leaves above an
oblate body, then couples four translated stations:

  result = test_toy_array_scattering(8,28,1e-5,true);

It reuses C4 quadrature and Fourier-mode solves, constructs square feed and
station scattering matrices with deterministic multilevel ID, and checks
the coupled array against the full corrected NRCCIE. See
test/ellipsoid/README_toy_rehearsal for definitions and measured errors.
Ground clearance is preserved geometrically; ground reflection is not yet
included. Generated data and figures are saved under test/results/.

Additional source includes the root-level leaf-mesh illustrations and
test_scattering_matrix_2d.m, an earlier 2D Helmholtz skeleton example.
slurm_jobs/run_leaves_nrccie.sh submits the current leaves example using
the Polar checkout paths specified in that script. diagnostics/ contains
historical diagnostic source; its README describes the retired dependencies.
